## 2026-06-13 EcosystemCandidate RegenerateInEditor test

- User questioned whether the tick/timer watcher is necessary because PCG should already support editor regeneration. Tested the preset-6 validation actor with the watcher explicitly stopped and `PCG_Style` set to `GenerationTrigger=GenerateOnLoad`, `RegenerateInEditor=true`, and `GenerateOnDropWhenTriggerOnDemand=true`.
- Important setup finding: setting those properties on the placed instance component can cause the live component to be renamed to `TRASH_PCGComponent_*` and recreated from the Blueprint component template. For a real test, `PCG_Style_GEN_VARIABLE` on `BP_Cubeless_PCG_EcosystemCandidate` was edited through `SubobjectDataSubsystem`, then the live component was set again. The asset was not saved.
- Regeneration finding: changing actor properties did trigger PCG regeneration with the current spline shape, so `RegenerateInEditor=true` is part of the right production direction. A temporary overgeneration spike to `79,703` instances was traced to bad test actor values (`EcosystemGrassSpawnRatio=205.051516`, `Tree=2.971015`, `Rock=1.787388`, `RibbonStep=55.706125`, `Width=1985`), not to the regenerate flag itself. Resetting to defaults (`RibbonStep=150`, `Width=2800`, `Grass=1.0`, `Tree=0.06`, `Rock=0.10`) returned output to `9,114` total instances on the current long test spline.
- Spline-change finding: direct Python `set_location_at_spline_point()` does not emit the same editor spline-handle edit event as a user drag. With watcher off and `RegenerateInEditor=true`, moving the endpoint from `[34000,46000,0]` to `[30000,50000,0]` did not refresh output by itself; `refresh_pcg_runtime_component()` also left the previous output bounds unchanged. This means automated validation still needs a native helper that performs the real editor spline edit notification, or the user must manually drag in the viewport to confirm the UI path.
- Structure finding: the current graph still reads ribbon width from spline point `Scale.Y`, while the artist-facing control is `EcosystemWidthCm`. Without the watcher, changing the actor width does not automatically synchronize existing spline point scale. Production cleanup should either move width sync into a Blueprint construction/editor hook or remove the hidden spline-scale dependency from the graph.
- Latest log check after the RegenerateInEditor test found no new `IsRotationNormalized`, `Assertion failed`, `Fatal`, or `LogPCG: Error` entries. Older Python probing errors remain in the log from API exploration.
