## 2026-06-17 PCG Dungeon V2 Editor Menu Regenerate Command

- Added a no-C++ editor command to `Plugins/CustomTools/Content/Python/ArtScripts/RegisterMenu.py`: `Cubeless > PCG Dungeon V2 > Regenerate From BP Controller`.
- Added the same command to the actor right-click menu as `Cubeless : Regenerate Dungeon V2 From BP Controller`.
- The command calls `CubelessDungeonPCGV2.begin_generation_refresh_with_bp_controller()`, so it reads the placed `MCP_Cubeless_Dungeon_V2_Controller` BP actor values, validates them, syncs bridge tags, and requests a fresh V2 NativeOutput generation without needing a PowerShell runner command.
- The BP controller read path now clamps out-of-range Details values before validation and writes the corrected value back to the placed actor. This was needed because the editor test found `DungeonBranchChancePercent=103`, while the supported range is `0..100`.
- The BP controller sync path now also resolves `DungeonRoomCount` before writing bridge tags. If the requested room count cannot pass layout validation for the current seed, it searches downward for the nearest passing room count and writes that corrected value back to the actor, preventing the editor menu from failing with a silent "not applied" result.
- Added `--allow-seed-suite-warning` to the V2 runner. BP/controller and `--set` refreshes enable the policy automatically; `--verify-existing-output` can opt into it explicitly when validating an already generated single-seed custom output. Preset/default verification remains strict by default.
- Direct Details panel `Call In Editor` button authoring was probed with a temporary Blueprint. Python could create a function graph, but the required Blueprint call-in-editor function flag/graph node editing path is not exposed reliably, so the project-safe implementation is the editor menu command unless a later C++/plugin route is approved.
