- Decision (route A): keep UDS source quality; disable the ~6 UDS-data modules by hand in the Niagara editor (`Kill_Particles_Outside_Area`, `KillParticlesBelowWaterLevel`, `WeatherParticle_KillSphere`, `Visibility_by_Camera_Distance`, `Camera_Particle_Depth`, `GetWaterLevel`, `Get_Cached_Particle_Path`). MCP/python expose no Niagara module disable/remove API, so this stays TA hand-work. BP repointed back to `NS_MCPRain`/`NS_MCPSnow` with the `User.Amount`→spawn contract.
- Repo durable doc: `systems/mcpweather.md` (wiring, verification, FX integration contract).
- FX final (route B, adopted): duplicated engine `DefaultSystem` (native Fountain) into `NS_Rain`/`NS_Snow`, `SpawnRate→User.Amount`, gravity rain -2500/snow -150, renderer materials `M_MCPRain_Particle`/`M_MCPSnow_Particle`, BP component template scale rain 0.25/snow 0.3, BP spawn multipliers rain×9000/snow×7000. PIE QA passed: both render as dense camera-following precipitation from BP defaults. Route A (UDS) shelved — no MCP API to disable Niagara modules. Sprite-size/velocity/spawn-box stay tool-blocked (particle-spawn-script), so thin rain streaks need manual Niagara work.
- Review caught a UDS dependency: the duplicated particle materials still referenced `/Game/UltraDynamicSky`. User confirmed UDS is not used, so removed it: deleted `NS_MCPRain`/`NS_MCPSnow` and `M_MCPRain_Particle`/`M_MCPSnow_Particle`, built self-contained `M_MCPRain_Soft`/`M_MCPSnow_Soft` (Unlit/Translucent, radial soft-dot opacity, engine-only), swapped NS_Rain/NS_Snow renderers. Re-audit: 0 external `/Game` references — fully self-contained. Both render as soft round particles in PIE.
- Editor-recovery note: rebuilding a renderer-referenced material via delete+recreate while PIE ran popped a blocking "Overwrite Existing Object" modal (game thread responsive but main tick paused → MCP timeouts). Recovered headlessly via Win32 `PostMessage(WM_CLOSE)` to the modal HWND; then edited materials in place (no delete) to avoid the collision. Lesson: stop PIE and edit assets in place rather than delete+recreate referenced assets.
- Tier 3 surface occlusion (OcclusionUseDF): was a dangling MPC flag with no consumer. Built helper `MF_MCP_Occlusion` (DistanceToNearestSurface at WorldPos+up*300, /300, saturate → roof detection; lerp(1, skyVis, MPC.OcclusionUseDF) gate; engine-only, self-contained). Injected into `MF_MCP_SurfaceWetness` and `MF_MCP_SnowCover` by multiplying the up-facing wetness/snow mask by the occlusion mask (via MCP material node tools by node_id; the MaterialFunctionCall output pin only syncs after re-setting MaterialFunction). PIE-verified with floor+half-roof: OcclusionUseDF=1 → dark (masked) rectangle under the roof, bright elsewhere; =0 → uniform (no occlusion). Requires `r.GenerateMeshDistanceFields=1` (confirmed) and a PIE/realtime context (GDF absent in non-PIE editor viewport). Particle-side occlusion (rain not falling under roofs) stays tool-blocked (Niagara particle script). Self-containment re-audit: still 0 external /Game refs.
